DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammppiicckk reads a PNM or PAM image stream as input.  It picks certain im‐
       ages  from the stream and copies them to a new image stream on Standard
       Output.

       You identify the images to pick by sequence number within  the  stream.
       Each  _i_m_a_g_e___s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e___n_u_m_b_e_r  is  a  decimal  sequence number, with zero
       meaning the first image.

       The arguments must be in increasing order, without duplicates.  The re‐
       sults  are  undefined if they are not.  (There are a number of enhance‐
       ments that might be made in future releases that  would  make  whatever
       ppaammppiicckk  does  today when you break this rule change).  ppaammppiicckk outputs
       the images in the same order as they appear in the input.  If you spec‐
       ify no sequence numbers, ppaammppiicckk outputs nothing.  If you specify a se‐
       quence number that is beyond what is in the input, ppaammppiicckk  fails  with
       an error message to that effect.

       ppaammppiicckk  always  reads  the entire input stream.  (This is helpful when
       the input stream is a pipe and whatever is feeding the  pipe  would  be
       upset if it filled up or broke).

       To see how many images, and what kind, are in a stream, use ppaammffiillee.

       To  extract  all  the images in a stream into separate named files, use
       ppaammsspplliitt.



